WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.100
Cinderella Four

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.080
What's going on, Director Hayato?

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.750
The Mayor of Hong Kong has ordered us
to leave the city.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.790
We're to leave sometime today.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.980
Guess I can understand why.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.620
If we're out by twelve midnight,
that's still today.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.690
But I believe there're
more items to load.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.490
Director, the stuff from
Luio & Co. has arrived.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.530
- Is that the final load?
- No, there's still more!

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:08.900
Hey!

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.270
Once you get a moment,
come and help us load!

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.240
Okay!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.110
Kamille.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.150
Mr. Amuro.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.280
You'll get scolded if Hayato
sees you fooling around.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.650
I'm not slacking off.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.640
I was thinking about something.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:29.350
About the girl you said you met
during the day?

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.920
It feels different from
falling in love.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.330
How should I put it...?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.390
It's a more tangible feeling.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.000
Can you understand what I'm getting at?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.900
In other words...

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.770
You've experienced this feeling,
haven't you?

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.400
If you're saying it's the feeling
of a Newtype, you're wrong.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.300
People with great insight are
capable of understanding each other...

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.840
...the first time they meet.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.840
Even the feeling of being pulled?

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:57.310
- Being pulled?
- Two men discussing secrets?

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.290
I can't keep you out of my sight,
can I, Kamille?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.550
It's not at all what you think.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.990
That's called love at first sight.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.650
What do you want?!

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.560
Kamille, that's dangerous.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.190
You're better off keeping a distance
from that girl.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.000
Why is that?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.770
There is no reason!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.100
Amuro!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.400
Let him go!

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.930
Leave Amuro alone.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.310
But...!

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.440
Mrs. Mirai.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.480
I'm aware that you fought with Amuro
back in the days of the White Base.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.650
Won't you tell me about the person
Amuro fought?

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.130
About Zeon's pilot?

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.060
That's a lie!

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.690
I can't say anything...

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.700
...if you already think you
know the truth.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:49.200
I'm worried for Amuro!

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.130
Unless I know more about him,
how can I care for him sufficiently?

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:57.080
You're carelessly jumping too deeply
into people's hearts.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.380
But right now, I believe I was only
talking of my own heart.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.480
What kind of enemy was that person?

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:06.690
I'm sorry.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.350
I don't know that much.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.410
But this person, Lalah, was responsible...

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:16.050
...for completely pulling Amuro away
from reality, even though she had died.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.490
Did he love her?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.620
They were enemies,
and hardly met each other.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.260
Do you think two such people
can love each other...

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.960
...enough to change their lives?

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.400
I think it's impossible.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.130
That was their relationship.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.140
<i>Four could be to me</i>
<i>what that person was to Amuro.</i>

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.040
What am I thinking about?!

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.490
Will it work?

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.470
Good.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.540
How's the booster working?

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:39.310
- It can be used any time!
- That's great!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.340
- Please.
- Th-Thank you.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.350
How do things look?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.890
I've changed programs for
the piloting system.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.050
- Good.
- However...!

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.150
We've been depending too much
on Cyber-Newtypes.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.460
But...!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.020
We can't afford not to utilize the power
of the Psyco Gundam.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:57.330
If Hong Kong should become a sea of fire
as a result, well, that can't be helped.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.660
Hong Kong is a leased territory
of the Federation Government.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.030
Earth is presently under the control
of the Titans.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.200
And a soldier's job is to abide
by his orders.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.240
Does that also go for
the Murasame Laboratory?

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:13.410
You'd be able to put more energy into
your research by working under the Titans.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.180
I wish you wouldn't make me waste
my time like this, Ensign Four.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.920
You're the one who left me behind.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.650
That's why I've come to get you now.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.860
Sergeant! Be more discreet
with your words.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.830
Yes, Number Four.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:38.260
Never call me that again.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.300
Who's there?!

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:43.910
Kamille.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.770
Somebody you know?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.310
What are you doing here?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.750
I thought I might be able to see you again.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.310
Sergeant, return alone.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:55.090
I'm not going back yet.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.180
Ensign.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.220
I have special orders from the Captain.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.560
Then I'll return by twelve midnight.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.470
You wouldn't mind giving me
that much time, would you?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:08.800
Twelve midnight?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.900
I ask that you forgive me for hitting you.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.170
I'd just like a little time right now.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:16.570
Very well.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.580
I'll explain that to the Captain.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:19.610
Thank you.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.280
However, I insist that you wear this.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.410
Goodbye.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.420
What's the matter?

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.460
It seems that we're enemies.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.290
Only according to lines adults have drawn.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.290
You're right.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.930
The Federation and the A.E.U.G.
are no different from each other.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.730
Just different uniforms.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.960
Hey, how does it feel
to pilot a mobile suit?

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.140
How does it feel?

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.170
Well, I'm only in it to fight, so...!

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.080
Right.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.200
You're right about that.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:26.940
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.270
Wh-What?

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:31.480
Kiss me.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.420
Sure.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.120
You're very kind.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.810
You see, I'm a war orphan.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.700
Shall I tell you the truth?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:08:59.840
About what?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.240
Do you like my name?

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.640
It's a great name. I like it.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.250
I hate it.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.690
Why? It has a nice ring to it.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.790
I was the fourth one in my laboratory,
and that's why I'm Four.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.460
Number Four.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.700
- What's your real name?
- I don't know.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.500
I have no memory of my past.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.810
I want to know about my past.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.740
That's what I've been searching for.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.710
But you can make as many memories
as you wish from this point on.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.840
- Are you sure about that?
- Four.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.570
How could they?!

00:09:58.810 --> 00:09:59.770
Kamille.

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:06.410
<i>This is the same feeling I had then.</i>

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.540
<i>Could Kamille be that person?</i>

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.550
The uniform's not the only difference!

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:12.590
The A.E.U.G. would never
do something like this!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.100
Who's piloting the Psyco Gundam?!

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:29.530
Four! Let's go to the Audhumla!

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.870
There's no reason why you should remain
with the Federation Forces.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.000
My memory...

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.100
My memory exists there.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.300
That airplane will bring me my memory!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.070
Four!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.510
I hate feeling lonely.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.380
I have no memories for comforting
myself in loneliness.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.280
It's something that someone
with parents cannot understand.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.320
Four.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:51.820
Four!

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:05.640
Four!

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.370
What's gotten into you?!

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.600
Can you tell who I am?

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.240
Can you tell?!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:17.950
Wait! Four!

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.780
Miss Stephanie's helicopter
is requesting permission to land!

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.620
We must send out our mobile suits first!

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.320
Get the Nemos ready, too!

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.990
Moving the Audhumla!

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:33.060
Rick Dias, ready for take-off!

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:33.900
I'm going!

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:35.660
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.910
Who could have invented
this kind of mobile suit?

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.750
We can't afford to
take care of the Sudori.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.710
Not the Mk. II?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.350
It uses a scattering beam cannon
and can float in the air!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.420
Is that Namicar piloting the Psyco Gundam
without my approval?!

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:35.220
No, it's Ben Wooder!

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.760
No other man would even think
of trying to operate it!

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.060
What's wrong with it?!

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:46.260
It stopped on its own! What happened?!

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.210
No, I can't destroy it here!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.640
Wh-What's this?

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.860
I'm not moving it!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:03.860
Wh-What's going on?!

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:07.750
Please notice me, Rick Dias!

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.160
That light.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:15.430
Kamille!

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:17.360
Is it Captain Amuro Ray?

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:21.770
D-Damn!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:22.710
Stop!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.240
I wouldn't move it like this!

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:26.440
Wh-What the...!

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.720
What's that light?

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.750
I get it, Namicar!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:45.460
You meant that the Psyco Gundam
belongs to a Cyber-Newtype, right?!

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.840
We've been looking for you, Ensign Four!

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.610
Thank you very much, Captain Wooder.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.350
Back up the Hizacks!
I'm sure you understand!

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:13.560
I understand.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:21.830
So a system has been completed that
connects the human will to a machine.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.600
Can't you answer me, Kamille?!

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:31.340
If you refuse to talk to me properly
about Newtypes...

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.280
...I need to find things out on my own!

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:35.880
I'm returning to the ship.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.810
Sortie at once with the Mk. II
to counterattack!

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.110
What took you so long?!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.550
Miss Stephanie.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.250
Kamille, are you taking the battles
of Karaba and the A.E.U.G. seriously?!

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.520
Of course I am!

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:53.360
That's why I'm fighting battles, right?!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.260
Then, don't leave at a time like this!

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.240
It's not like I left to fool around!

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:58.290
Kamille!

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.640
That boy is a little different,
isn't it?

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:02.910
Think so?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:05.600
She's like a female Wong Lee!!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.080
A man can't go out to die
just because he's been slapped!

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:10.210
Gundam Mk. II, taking off!

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.390
Captain Amuro's quick!

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.030
Nemo unit, protect the Audhumla!

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.570
Mk. II, don't fall behind!

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:32.540
Roger!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.940
This damn city! This damn city!

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:42.780
What good is this damn city anyway?!

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:50.890
What good are new memories if I can't
get the memories of my past back?!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.800
Just burn...! Everything...!

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:09.400
That place...!

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:23.450
I'll tear you apart!

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.220
Stop it!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:34.660
Wh-Why you're...!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.470
You're kidding!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:50.580
Have you been created to make me suffer?!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.480
Four, is it you?

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.740
I hate you!

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:05.430
You mustn't fight, Four!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.430
Not you!

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:13.000
S-Stop it!

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.810
Four, come to your senses.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.470
Four, you mustn't fight!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.870
It's because things like this exist
that I must suffer eternally!

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.450
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.650
You're going to get yourself killed!

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:45.030
Captain, please stop it!

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.630
Four, can you tell? It's me, Kamille!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:51.370
Are you telling me
to stop attacking, Kamille?

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.690
Four, can you hear me?!

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:07.160
I know it's you!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.060
Open up, Four!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:14.930
Four!

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.870
I want my memory.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.900
I want to know more about myself.

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.130
Four, come out of there.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:22.970
I was told that the Murasame Laboratory...

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.380
...would reinstate my memory
if I defeat the Mk. II.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.410
They're lying!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:30.420
Do you really believe they'll make good
on such a promise?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.580
Is it wrong to want to know more
about myself?!

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.180
Four, come to space with me.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.220
To space?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:42.120
With the technology of the A.E.U.G., Four,
I'm sure your memory can be reinstated.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.160
Four!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.120
They can't fix something
out in space...

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:46.690
...that couldn't be fixed at the Laboratory!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.100
We won't know that until we give it a try!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:50.930
It's useless.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:51.970
Four!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.770
<i>Kamille, you know everything about me!</i>

00:18:56.840 --> 00:19:00.110
It's because there's someone
who knows you that you're able to live life!

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.080
Then stop being my enemy!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:04.810
Be kind to me!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.320
I don't like being pushed around!

00:19:16.100 --> 00:19:18.090
You'll only end up
committing more crimes!

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:18.990
Four!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.540
Captain?!

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.830
<i>I'm destroying the system.</i>

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:31.230
The combat system is forcing
the pilot to fight!

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:34.680
But the pilot is Four!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:35.710
Where is it?

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:37.340
Where is the system's core?

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:38.910
Where is the system's...?

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:49.750
Did I get it?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:57.870
Four!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.280
What is it?!

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:23.120
Why get in my way?!

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.540
I'll make her do it.

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:40.310
But...!

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:45.910
If Four is a complete Cyber-Newtype,
she'll still be able to fight.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:51.520
Right now, our priority
is to hunt down the Audhumla.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.520
Are you really going to go?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.920
I'll go, perhaps to India
on the Coral Oriental.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:00.390
The last thing I want to do
is get in Bright's way.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:02.790
I see.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.300
And Miss Stephanie says
she'll give us her support.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.500
Amuro, where's Kamille?

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.640
That's too bad. I was hoping
to talk to him one last time.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.320
Take good care of him.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.920
I promised that I'd send him to space.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.420
I will make good on my promise.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:26.550
But don't be reckless.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:28.890
I will not die in vain.

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.660
Mrs. Mirai. We should be going.

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:31.700
Right.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:36.400
- Let's get on first.
- Oh, thank you.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.240
Beltorchika.

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:45.740
There's no sense rushing things.

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:50.470
It's the same with any relationship
between two people.

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:53.990
It's best to take your time
to understand one another.

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:56.420
I don't understand.

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:58.890
You will when you get older.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:21:59.930
Good-bye.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:16.740
What did Mirai tell you?

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:20.980
Women's talk.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:50.710
Even during battle, Four is aware
of what she will eventually choose.

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:54.510
Perhaps this is the nature
of human existence.

00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:58.850
Although Kamille realizes the connection
between his mind and Four's...

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:01.150
...he still attempts to escape to space.

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:07.450
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Heated Escape".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
The Heated Escape

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:12.430
You will see the tears of time.
